## 1. Local Machine & Multi-Agent Throughput (Zero-Cost, Immediate)

### 1.1 Git 50× Index Acceleration (Already Active Locally)
Because `store/` holds tens of thousands of content-addressed objects, standard `git status` rescans the filesystem on every command (~5.8s). Enabling macOS/Linux FSMonitor + untracked cache drops `git status` to **~0.12s (48.5× faster)**:

```bash
git config core.fsmonitor true
git config core.untrackedCache true
git config feature.manyFiles true
git config core.preloadIndex true
git config core.commitGraph true
git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths
```

### 1.2 Automatic `hx merge` Git Driver for `store/ROOT/root`
When multiple agents or branches modify distinct modules concurrently, `store/<hash>/*` objects never conflict (content-addressed), while the 1-line `store/ROOT/root` pointer always conflicts. Registering the compiled `hx merge` semilattice merger eliminates manual root merges forever:

```bash
# Build unified native super-CLI once
./build/cubical lib/hx.hypercubical /tmp/e_hx.hypercubical
clang -std=c11 -O3 -fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all -o /usr/local/bin/hx /tmp/hx.c

# Register custom 3-way merge driver locally
git config merge.hxroot.name "Hyperactivity 3-way semilattice store root merger"
git config merge.hxroot.driver 'sh -c "
  B=\$(cat \$1); O=\$(cat \$2); T=\$(cat \$3);
  hx merge store/\$B/root store/\$O/root store/\$T/root /tmp/hx-merged.root &&
  H=\$(./build/cubical --put-root /tmp/hx-merged.root) &&
  printf \"%s\n\" \"\$H\" > \$2
" -- %O %A %B'
```

### 1.3 Isolated Worktrees for Parallel Agents
Give every concurrent agent its own git worktree backed by shared object storage so `.cubical-store/index` never collides:

```bash
git worktree add ../hx-agent-1 -b feat/silicon-eda main
git worktree add ../hx-agent-2 -b feat/pouw-mesh main
```

